3:Te93,<h2>Introduction</h2>
<p>Knee pain can significantly impact your quality of life, making it difficult to perform everyday activities. For many individuals, this discomfort is due to cartilage damage. As we approach 2026, advancements in medical science are providing more effective solutions for cartilage repair surgery in the knee. If you're in Hyderabad and experiencing persistent knee pain, understanding the latest surgical options can be crucial to finding the right treatment.</p>

<h2>Understanding Cartilage Damage</h2>
<p>Cartilage is a resilient and smooth elastic tissue, a rubber-like padding that covers and protects the ends of long bones at the joints. In the knee, healthy cartilage enables smooth movement and acts as a shock absorber. However, injuries or degenerative conditions like osteoarthritis can lead to cartilage damage, causing pain, stiffness, and mobility issues. Understanding the extent of the damage is essential in determining the appropriate treatment approach.</p>

<h2>Types of Cartilage Repair Surgery</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Microfracture Surgery:</strong> This technique involves creating small fractures in the underlying bone. This process helps stimulate the growth of new cartilage, offering pain relief and improved joint function.</li>
<li><strong>Autologous Chondrocyte Implantation (ACI):</strong> A more advanced procedure, ACI involves collecting a small sample of your cartilage cells, expanding them in a lab, and re-implanting them into the damaged area, allowing natural cartilage to regrow.</li>
<li><strong>Osteochondral Autograft Transplantation:</strong> This involves transferring cartilage and underlying bone from a non-weight-bearing area of a patient's knee to the damaged area, which can provide effective pain relief and improved joint movement.</li>
<li><strong>Stem Cell Therapy:</strong> An emerging option, this involves injecting stem cells into the knee, stimulating the repair of damaged cartilage and potentially providing long-term relief.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Treatment Options</h2>
<p>The choice of surgery depends on the size and location of the cartilage defect, the patient's age and activity level, and any underlying health conditions. Despite several available options, consulting with an expert orthopedic surgeon such as Dr. B Harsha Vardhana Reddy at Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Hyderabad, is essential to determine the most suitable procedure for your condition.</p>

<h2>Why Choose Dr. Harsha at Apollo Hospitals, Hyderabad?</h2>
<p>Dr. B Harsha Vardhana Reddy is a renowned Senior Consultant Orthopedic Surgeon with extensive experience in knee surgeries. Patients at Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Hyderabad, benefit from the hospital's state-of-the-art facilities and Dr. Harsha's personalized approach to treatment. His commitment to delivering exceptional care ensures that patients receive the latest in cartilage repair surgeries tailored to their specific needs.</p>

<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<p><strong>Q: What is the recovery time for cartilage repair surgery?</strong></p>
<p>A: Recovery time varies depending on the type of surgery and individual patient factors, but generally, it ranges from a few weeks to several months. Physical therapy is crucial for optimal recovery.</p>
<p><strong>Q: Are there non-surgical options for cartilage repair?</strong></p>
<p>A: Yes, options such as physical therapy, injections, and lifestyle changes may be recommended for mild cartilage damage. However, severe cases often require surgical intervention.</p>

<h2>Book Your Appointment</h2>
<p>Call Dr. Harsha at <strong>+91 99599 64567</strong> or visit Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Nanakramguda, Hyderabad.</p>5:["slug","best-cartilage-repair-surgery-knee-guide-2026-hyderabad","d"]
